  German translation of values/strings.xml.

  Placeholders are POSITIONAL (%1$s / %1$d) and keep their numbers.
  Apostrophes and quotation marks are written RAW: Compose Multiplatform only
  unescapes \uXXXX, \n, \t and \\, so a backslash would reach the UI.
  "LatentJam" and "SMART" are names and stay untranslated.

  Terminology follows real players (Spotify, YouTube Music, Apple Music):
  Titel, Warteschlange, Zufallswiedergabe, Playlist, Bibliothek.
  The app addresses the user informally (du), as German music apps do.
  Quotation marks are the German „…“.
  Note: "Titel" is invariant in the plural, so both CLDR categories of
  count_tracks are identical by design — that is correct German.
-->
